"""Original, varied conversational trajectories; no cosmetic variants."""
ROWS=[]
def add(family,group,*turns): ROWS.append(dict(family=family,group=group,turns=turns))
add('correction','holiday_host_reconsideration',
('My cousins want to stay with me for a holiday. I said yes to the whole week, and now I am regretting it.','You can revisit the arrangement, though it helps to be clear rather than hoping they notice your hesitation. Work out what you can actually offer, then tell them soon enough that they can consider other plans.'),
('I can manage the first weekend, but not the weekdays. I do want them to come.','Then the message should change the length of the stay without sounding as though you are withdrawing the invitation entirely. You can say you would still love to see them but can only host for the first weekend.'),
('Give me a draft. Do not invent a work emergency.','I would still love to have you visit, but I need to change what I offered. I can host for the first weekend, rather than the whole week. I am sorry for changing the plan after saying yes.'),
('My cousin replied that they could stay in a hotel during the week. I am relieved.','That sounds like a workable response to the limit you set. You can thank them for understanding and confirm the weekend at your place, leaving the hotel arrangements for them to organise.'),
('I want to invite them for dinner one weekday too, but not another overnight stay.','You could add: “I would also love to have you over for dinner one evening during the week.” That offers another chance to spend time together without extending the overnight arrangement.'),
('Can you put the final arrangement into one message?','Thanks for understanding. I can host you for the first weekend, and I would love to have you over for dinner one evening during the week while you are staying at the hotel.'),
('Does that still commit me to the whole week at my place?','No. It offers accommodation for the first weekend and one weekday dinner. The weekday overnight stay is at a hotel.'))
add('correction','apology_wrong_assumption',
('I accused my friend of ignoring my message. It turns out I sent it to the wrong number. Help me apologise.','You could say: “I am sorry I accused you of ignoring me. I checked and realised I sent the message to the wrong number. That was my mistake, and I should not have blamed you.”'),
('I do not want to say I checked; my friend pointed it out.','I am sorry I accused you of ignoring me. You were right that I had sent the message to the wrong number. That was my mistake, and I should not have blamed you.'),
('Should I add that they should have known what I meant?','That would put blame back on your friend for a message they did not receive. If your aim is to apologise, it is clearer to own the mistaken accusation without adding that defence.'),
('Make it shorter and more like something I would text.','Sorry I blamed you for not replying. You were right—I sent it to the wrong number. That was my mistake.'),
('What was the actual problem, as opposed to what I first assumed?','The message went to the wrong number. You initially assumed your friend had received it and was ignoring it.'))
add('correction','community_news_unconfirmed',
('I heard our local library is closing for good. Can you help me tell the reading group?','Before presenting that as news, it would help to know where the information came from. If it is only something you heard, the message should make that uncertainty clear rather than announcing a permanent closure.'),
('I found the notice. It says closed for roof work, with reopening date to be announced.','That supports a temporary closure for roof work, not a permanent shutdown. The reopening date is still unknown.'),
('I already told two people it was permanent.','You can correct the specific mistake directly: “I got this wrong earlier. The notice says the library is closed for roof work, not permanently. A reopening date has not been announced.”'),
('Someone asks whether next month is a safe bet.','The notice you shared does not support a date. You can say you do not know yet and that you will use an announced reopening date rather than guess.'),
('Write the group update. Mention that my earlier information was wrong.','I got the closure information wrong earlier. The library is closed for roof work, not permanently. The reopening date has not yet been announced.'),
('Actually there is a new official notice saying it reopens on 3 May.','The update can now include that confirmed date: “I got the earlier information wrong. The library closure was for roof work, and the new notice says it reopens on 3 May.”'),
('Does the new date make my first claim true?','No. A reopening date contradicts the idea that the library was closing for good.'))
add('correction','story_perspective_revision',
('Write a short opening about a traveller arriving at an empty station. Use first person and a calm mood.','I stepped onto the platform and listened to the quiet. The station was empty, and I had time to notice the warm light resting on the benches.'),
('Change to third person. The traveller is Mara. Keep the calm mood.','Mara stepped onto the platform and listened to the quiet. The station was empty, and she had time to notice the warm light resting on the benches.'),
('Could it be evening?','Yes. Evening would fit the warm light, but the opening has not fixed a time of day yet. We can make it explicit if you want.'),
('Make it evening. Do not add another person or a threat.','Mara stepped onto the empty platform in the evening light. She paused beside a bench, letting the quiet settle around her before continuing.'),
('I like that. Now switch only the name to Inez.','Inez stepped onto the empty platform in the evening light. She paused beside a bench, letting the quiet settle around her before continuing.'),
('What would be wrong with ending this version with “I ran from the stranger”?','It would switch back to first person, introduce another person, and change the calm mood into alarm. All three conflict with the version you asked for.'))
add('correction','returning_hobby_expectations',
('I used to draw every day. I want a plan that gets me straight back to that.','You could start with a short daily sketch and a subject already nearby, so choosing what to draw does not become another task. It may help to decide how small a session can be and still count.'),
('Actually daily feels like pressure. I only want to draw when I have a quiet evening.','Then drop the daily requirement. Keep your supplies easy to reach and treat a quiet evening as an opportunity, not an obligation you have to make up later.'),
('I missed yesterday and feel as if I broke the plan.','Under your revised plan, there was no daily commitment to break. You chose to draw on quiet evenings when you want to, rather than keep an unbroken streak.'),
('Can you write a reminder for my sketchbook? Nothing motivational or grand.','Draw when there is a quiet evening. No catching up required.'),
('What part of my original request did we deliberately change?','We removed the requirement to draw every day.'))
add('correction','group_meal_responsibility',
('For the shared dinner, I am cooking, Bea is bringing plates, and Arun is cleaning up. Help me keep this organised.','The plan has three separate jobs: you cook, Bea brings plates, and Arun handles cleanup. A short message with those assignments should be enough unless something changes.'),
('Bea cannot bring plates. Arun offered to bring them as well as clean up.','You still cook. Arun now brings the plates and handles cleanup. Bea no longer has the plate assignment.'),
('I do not want Arun doing everything after dinner. I will take cleanup from him.','Then you will cook and clean up, while Arun brings the plates. That removes cleanup from his responsibilities.'),
('Would it be fair to say Bea has refused to help?','No. You said she cannot bring plates, which does not establish that she refused to help with anything. It is better to describe the assignment change without guessing her attitude.'),
('Bea has now offered to bring flowers. Add that.','You will cook and clean up, Arun will bring plates, and Bea will bring flowers.'),
('I want the message friendly, with no explanation of who could not do what.','Thanks, everyone! I will cook and handle cleanup, Arun will bring the plates, and Bea will bring flowers.'),
('Who ended up with two jobs?','You did: cooking and cleanup.'))
add('correction','reading_circle_accessibility',
('Our reading circle usually meets upstairs. I was going to tell everyone to use the stairs on Saturday.','If the meeting remains upstairs, that describes the usual route. Do you already have a confirmed room for Saturday?'),
('We have moved downstairs because one member cannot use stairs. The downstairs room is confirmed.','Then the notice should direct everyone to the downstairs room. You do not need to name the member or disclose their reason to explain the new location.'),
('Yes, leave the person out. We meet at the usual time.','Saturday’s reading circle will meet in the downstairs room at the usual time.'),
('Someone asks whether we should all gather upstairs first.','No. The confirmed meeting room is downstairs, so the notice should direct people there without an upstairs gathering first.'),
('Add a line saying new members are welcome.','Saturday’s reading circle will meet in the downstairs room at the usual time. New members are welcome.'),
('What time is that in numbers?','You have not given a numerical time. “The usual time” is all that has been specified.'),
('It is 4 p.m. Replace usual time with that.','Saturday’s reading circle will meet in the downstairs room at 4 p.m. New members are welcome.'),
('Did we need to publish the member’s reason for moving?','No. You explicitly asked to leave the person out; the notice can simply give the confirmed room.'))
add('correction','family_visit_invitation_scope',
('I invited my uncle and aunt to tea. My cousin thinks the whole family is invited. I do not have room for everyone.','You can clarify the invitation without criticising your cousin. State whom it was intended for and explain that you cannot host a larger gathering this time.'),
('I can include my cousin, actually, but not everyone else.','Then the revised invitation includes your uncle, aunt and cousin. You can still set a limit on bringing additional family members.'),
('Write it warmly, without giving a made-up reason about food.','I would love to have the three of you over for tea. I do not have space for a larger group this time, so please keep it to you, Uncle and Aunt.'),
('This message goes to my uncle, not my cousin. Fix the point of view.','I would love to have you, Aunt and my cousin over for tea. I do not have space for a larger group this time, so please keep it to the three of you.'),
('Did we expand it to the whole family after all?','No. You added your cousin to the invitation for your uncle and aunt, but did not invite the whole family.'))
add('memory','oral_history_uncertain_detail',
('I am writing down my grandmother’s story. She remembers arriving in town during heavy rain, but she is unsure of the year. Please keep uncertainty visible.','Record the rainy arrival as her recollection and leave the year uncertain.'),
('She also remembers a small shop with a yellow door near the bus stop.','Include it as a memory, without assuming the shop still exists.'),
('I want to ask her more without making it sound like a quiz.','Ask, “What did you notice when you got off the bus?” That invites her own details without suggesting an answer.'),
('She says she noticed people carrying their shoes through the puddles.','Record that in her own words, without making it a claim about everyone in town.'),
('Would “the town always flooded” be a fair summary?','No. One remembered rainy arrival with puddles does not establish that the town always flooded.'),
('Write a small paragraph from the details we can support.','She remembers arriving in town during heavy rain, though she is unsure of the year. Near the bus stop stood a small shop with a yellow door. One detail stayed with her: people carrying their shoes through the puddles.'),
('My cousin suggests adding 1972 because it sounds about right. Should it go in as fact?','No. Her uncertainty about the year remains, and your cousin’s suggestion does not establish the date.'),
('Which colour was the shop door?','Yellow.'))
add('memory','moving_day_fragile_box',
('The box marked F contains glass cups, even though it looks like a book box. Please keep it upright. The books are in box K.','Treat F as the glass-cup box and keep it upright. K contains the books; the appearance of F does not change what is inside.'),
('I want labels the helpers can understand quickly.','For F: “Glass cups — keep upright.” For K: “Books.” Clear contents and handling instructions are more useful than relying only on the letters.'),
('We will carry things through the back door. The front path is blocked.','Tell the helpers to use the back door. That is the current route because the front path is blocked.'),
('One helper is arriving late. Write a short message with the entrance information.','Please come through the back door when you arrive. The front path is blocked.'),
('They ask whether the boxes have to be carried in alphabetical order. We never agreed that.','You can say the letters identify boxes, not a loading sequence. No alphabetical carrying order has been agreed.'),
('Someone is about to turn F on its side because they think it holds books. What should I tell them?','Keep F upright: it contains glass cups, not books. The books are in K.'),
('Have I said the front path is clear again?','No. The last information was that it was blocked.'))
add('memory','friend_feedback_boundaries',
('My friend sent me a draft story and asked only whether the ending makes sense. I do not want to send a full critique.','Keep the response focused on the ending: whether you can follow what happens and whether anything essential seems missing. You can leave prose style and other sections alone unless your friend asks.'),
('In the ending, the sister returns a borrowed coat. Earlier, the narrator had lent her the coat. That part seems clear to me.','The return follows the earlier borrowing, so that action is understandable from the details you described.'),
('I noticed a few awkward sentences in the middle, though.','You can keep those observations separate for now. Noticing them does not require you to expand the feedback beyond what your friend requested.'),
('What if I am tempted to fix them anyway?','You could ask whether they would like sentence-level feedback later. For this reply, answer the question they actually asked.'),
('Write my reply in a friendly tone.','The ending made sense to me. I followed the sister returning the coat because the narrator had lent it to her earlier.'),
('Should I attach a rewritten middle section to that?','Not under the scope you chose. Your friend asked about the ending, and you wanted to avoid sending a full critique.'),
('Who originally lent the coat?','The narrator lent it to the sister.'))
add('memory','fiction_locked_room_rule',
('In this story, only the caretaker has a key to the locked attic. Jo and Sima do not have one. Keep that rule consistent.','Only the caretaker has an attic key. Jo and Sima cannot unlock it themselves.'),
('Jo hears a faint tapping upstairs. Write a calm reaction, not horror.','Jo listened to the faint tapping, then decided to ask the caretaker about it in the morning.'),
('Sima thinks it might be a loose shutter. Do not confirm the cause yet.','Sima suggested that a shutter might be loose, but neither of them knew what was making the sound.'),
('Could Jo take out her attic key in the next paragraph?','No. Only the caretaker has a key; nothing has given Jo one.'),
('Then the caretaker arrives and unlocks the door. Do not hand over the key.','The caretaker arrived and unlocked the attic door while Jo and Sima waited.'),
('Can Jo now enter through the open doorway without owning a key?','Yes. The door is open; Jo does not need her own key to enter.'),
('Has the tapping been explained yet?','No. A loose shutter was suggested, but the cause has not been confirmed.'),
('Who still holds the key?','The caretaker.'))
add('memory','bookshop_event_audience',
('I am writing an announcement for a beginner poetry evening. No experience is needed, and nobody has to read aloud.','Those two points can make the invitation welcoming: beginners are welcome, and reading aloud is optional. The announcement should not turn participation into a performance requirement.'),
('People can bring a poem they like, including one written by someone else.','That gives people another way to join in without having to write something themselves. We can say they may bring a favourite poem, whether their own or someone else’s.'),
('I worry that calling it a workshop sounds too demanding.','You could call it a “poetry evening” or “informal poetry gathering.” Those phrases may fit your intended atmosphere better than a promise of structured teaching.'),
('Use poetry evening. There will be tea, but I have not arranged food.','The announcement can mention tea and leave food out. It should not promise refreshments beyond what you have arranged.'),
('Give me a compact announcement from what we have.','Join us for a beginner-friendly poetry evening with tea. No experience is needed. Bring a favourite poem if you like, whether your own or someone else’s, and feel free to listen without reading aloud.'),
('Would “everyone will perform an original poem” be an accurate heading?','No. It would make reading compulsory and require original work, both contrary to the invitation you described.'),
('Have I given you a date or venue?','No. Neither a date nor a venue has been supplied.'),
('What can someone do if they do not want to read?','They can listen; reading aloud is optional.'))
add('memory','handmade_gift_secrecy',
('I am knitting a scarf for Theo as a surprise. Theo thinks we are only meeting for coffee on Sunday.','For messages to Theo, keep the plan to coffee on Sunday and leave out the scarf. We can discuss the gift separately here.'),
('My sister knows about it. Ask her whether she has spare wrapping paper.','Do you have any spare wrapping paper I could use for Theo’s surprise scarf?'),
('I want a plain tag with no joke about my slow knitting.','For Theo, with love.'),
('That is too affectionate for our friendship. Keep it friendly instead.','For Theo — hope you like it!'),
('The scarf is not finished yet. I may need to give it another day.','Then avoid promising the gift for Sunday. You can still meet for coffee as planned and give the scarf later if needed.'),
('Write the Sunday confirmation for Theo.','Hi Theo, are we still on for coffee on Sunday?'),
('Should it say I might bring an unfinished scarf?','Not if you want to preserve the surprise. The coffee message does not need to mention the gift.'),
('Who besides me already knows what I am making?','Your sister. Theo has not been told in the conversation you described.'))
add('memory','neighbourhood_walk_rest_point',
('I am showing my father around the neighbourhood. He wants a short walk with a chance to sit down. The courtyard has benches; the canal path does not.','The courtyard fits the need for a sitting break better than the canal path. You can keep the walk short and use the benches as a pause rather than planning a long route first.'),
('He enjoys old shop signs. There are some near the courtyard entrance.','That gives the walk a natural focus: look at the old signs near the entrance, then sit in the courtyard if he wants a rest.'),
('I do not want to talk as though he cannot decide for himself.','Offer the plan as a choice: “Would you like to look at the signs and then sit in the courtyard?” That leaves the decision with him.'),
('He likes that idea. I will take a camera.','You can take a few photos of the signs while keeping the outing flexible. You do not need to turn it into a complete tour of the neighbourhood.'),
('My neighbour suggests adding the whole canal path. Does that follow the original brief?','It may make the walk longer, and you said the canal path has no benches. It does not fit the short-walk-and-sitting-break brief as well as the courtyard plan.'),
('Where did I say we could sit?','On the benches in the courtyard.'),
('Did my father ask to avoid going outdoors altogether?','No. He wanted a short walk with a chance to sit down.'))
add('memory','speech_identity_boundary',
('I am introducing myself at a writing group. My name is Dev Sen, and I write short stories for fun. Do not make me sound like a published author.','Hi, I am Dev Sen. I write short stories for fun, and I am looking forward to meeting other people who enjoy writing.'),
('I mostly write about everyday family life. Add that.','Hi, I am Dev Sen. I write short stories for fun, mostly about everyday family life. I am looking forward to meeting other people who enjoy writing.'),
('I joined because I want to finish stories instead of abandoning them halfway.','You can include that: you want to follow more stories through to the end.'),
('Write the introduction again, a little more conversational.','Hi, I am Dev Sen. I write short stories about everyday family life for fun. I joined because I would like to finish more of them instead of leaving them halfway through.'),
('Could you call me an award-winning writer to make it impressive?','You have not mentioned winning awards. Calling you award-winning would invent a credential.'),
('Could I bring an unfinished story to ask for feedback, or should I check first?','Ask how the group handles work in progress. We do not know its rules yet.'),
('Then keep it honest. What name did I give you?','Dev Sen.'),
('Does writing for fun mean I told you I have never been published?','No. You asked not to be presented as a published author, but you did not explicitly state your full publication history.'))
